SUMMARY:Monte Rio Redwoods 
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nThis is one of My Favorite local places to hik
 e. There are spectacular views of the Willow Creek watershed and miles of 
 hiking trails thru redwood forests dappled with sunlight.\n**This Trailhea
 d Has Very Limited Parking.**\n**You Must Have Zero No Shows to Attend.**\
 n**Everyone will start on the Waitlist.**\n**Please Do Not just show up fo
 r this hike!!!**\n\n**\\*Important Notice\\***\nIf you've enjoyed hiking w
 ith this group follow me as I move Go Wild Hikers to a new platform by the
  end of May\, called Heylo at - [https://heylo.com/invite/PpURbZWX](https:
 //heylo.com/invite/PpURbZWX)\nClick on the link above to join.\n\n**Where 
 We Meet/Important Directions**\nDue to limited parking and the desire to a
 ccommodate as many hikers as possible everyone must carpool!\n**Meet and b
 e ready to leave by \\*830am\\* from the commuter parking lot at the corne
 r of Graton Rd. & Main St. in Occidental.**\nGive yourself plenty of time 
 to arrive\, it often takes longer than you think. Especially this one!\n\n
 **The Hike**\nFern Springs\, Eastside\, Deadwood\, Koerber\, Upper Freeze 
 Out\, Blair Witch\, West Panties and East Panties trails - A loop hike\nLe
 ngth - +/-5.25 miles/8.45 kilometers\nElevation change - +/-985 feet/252 m
 eters\nDifficulty - 7+/10 moderately strenuous\nExposures - 40% sun /60% s
 hade - rocky\, poison oak\, ticks and insects.\nBring plenty of water. At 
 least 68 oz. /2 liters.\nDogs - No\, only because we're car pooling.\nFaci
 lities at trail head - None! Plan ahead.\nCost - $5 cash\nParking - **Meet
  and be ready to leave by 830am from the commuter parking lot at the corne
 r of Graton Rd. & Main St. in Occidental.**\nRemember to wear appropriate 
 hiking shoes\, bring plenty of water\, snack/lunch\, layered clothing & tr
 ekking poles.\nPlease Do Not Use Any scented products the day of a group h
 ike!\nOf course\, we will all look out for each other but ultimately\, hik
 ers are responsible for their own safety and well-being during hikes.\n\n*
 *After Hike Gathering**\nWild Flour Bakery\n140 Bohemian Hwy\, Freestone\,
  CA 95472\n(707) 874-2938\n[https://wildflourbread.com/](https://wildflour
 bread.com/)\n\n**When We Meet**\nSunday May 3\, 2026\n8:30 am - 12:00 pm\n
 If your plans change after you sign up even if you're on the waitlist\, pl
 ease update your RSVP.\nDo Not Attend if you are sick\, running a fever\, 
 were exposed to or have tested positive for Covid-19 or any other contagio
 n!\nHike may be changed\, rescheduled or cancelled in case of excessive he
 at\, rain\, smoke/AQI\, illness\, zombie apocalypse etc... Check your emai
 l the night before for any possible changes.
